## The --no-sandbox evidence run

It is a low and bounded risk.
The run was one local render of one fixed HTML file to /tmp.
No file outside measure records contains no-sandbox.
No live code calls pagedjs-cli; only package.json declares it.
The round 11 driver rendered both lesson PDFs without that flag and matched round 11.
Dashboard live code reaches the browser through lib/print/render.ts, not through pagedjs-cli.
One point stays: that HTML still loads an unpinned unpkg pagedjs script, so remote script ran with the OS sandbox off. This is B-D1-2.

